### direct call to payment-service
GET http://localhost:9005/payments/

### same call through the API Gateway
GET http://localhost:8080/payments/

### create a Stripe Checkout session for an order
### amount is in poisha (1/100 taka), so 25000 = BDT 250.00. Minimum is 10000 (BDT 100.00) -
### Stripe rejects amounts that convert to under ~$0.50, so a small poisha amount can be rejected.
POST http://localhost:9005/payments/checkout-session
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "order-123",
  "userId": "user-456",
  "amount": 25000,
  "currency": "bdt",
  "description": "FoodSloth order #123"
}

### open the "checkoutUrl" from the response above in a browser and pay with test card 4242 4242 4242 4242,
### any future expiry date, any CVC, any postal code.
### Stripe then redirects the browser to /payments/checkout-success, which verifies the session,
### updates the payment status, best-effort notifies order-service, and shows a confirmation page.

### manually verify a session (useful if you're not running the Stripe CLI webhook listener
### and didn't go through the browser success redirect)
GET http://localhost:9005/payments/session/{{sessionId}}/verify

### fetch a payment by its Mongo id
GET http://localhost:9005/payments/{{paymentId}}

### fetch the payment for a given order
GET http://localhost:9005/payments/order/order-123

### fetch all payments for a given user
GET http://localhost:9005/payments/user/user-456

### refund a succeeded payment
POST http://localhost:9005/payments/{{paymentId}}/refund
